tility":0.12299570920341668,"_gp_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":79.1,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":-0.10634101474823335,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":3,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":33.3,"_gate_spread":0.10794393976534196,"_gp_spread":true,"_score_spread":54.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":1.1200377113635713,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":-0.2643035621357152,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":0.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.12388972555758204,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":0.0,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":0.04244964079452407,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":46.2,"_gate_fcf_durability":-0.07057231605203562,"_gp_fcf_durability":false,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-0.011490720295668628,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":38.5,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.04253101726091505,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":58.4,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.011867768621134034,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":64.8,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.008375279642058166,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":86.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.06343,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":42.3,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Polaris Inc. designs, engineers, manufactures, and markets powersports vehicles in the United States, Canada, and internationally. It operates through three segments: Off Road, On Road, and Marine. The company offers off-road vehicles (ORVs), including all-terrain vehicles and side-by-side vehicles; military and commercial ORVs; snowmobiles; motorcycles; moto-roadsters; quadricycles; and pontoon and deck boats. It also provides source parts, garments, and accessories, such as helmets, jackets, gloves, pants, and hats; and snowmobile accessories comprising covers, traction products, reverse kits, electric starters, tracks, pull-behinds, bags, and windshields, as well as gear and apparel for its snowmobiles consisting of helmets, jackets, goggles, gloves, boots, bibs, pants, and hats. In addition, the company offers ORV accessories, including winches, bumper/brushguards, plows, racks, wheels and tires, cab systems, lighting and audio systems, cargo box accessories, and tracks, as well as replacement parts and lubricants. Further, it provides motorcycle accessories, such as performance enhancements, saddle bags, handlebars, backrests, exhausts, windshields, seats, and various chrome accessories, as well as light duty hauling and passenger vehicles. The company sells its products through dealers and distributors, as well as online. The company was formerly known as Polaris Industries Inc. Polaris Inc. was founded in 1945 and is headquartered in Medina, Minnesota.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Michael Todd Speetzen | CEO & Director | Age 56 | Compensation: $4.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 14K people. Revenue per employee of $493K ranks in the above the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers, improving at 9%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $38K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 8\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Polaris Inc. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $3.6B market cap on $7.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -6% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 20% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 11-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, and 24% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $558M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 8 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","Accruals are elevated at -24.7% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -2.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 4.3% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 6.3% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (15.8% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 368% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins softening -1.1pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Operating margins 12% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 19% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Polaris (PII) Returns To Profit As Valuation Debate Heats Up","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/consumer-durables/nyse-pii/polaris/news/polaris-pii-returns-to-profit-as-valuation-debate-heats-up","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793644166.205,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.94,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is Polaris (NYSE:PII) Finding Its Footing?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/automobile/is-polaris-nysepii-finding-its-footing","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793594520.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.103,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"What Polaris (PII)'s Raised Guidance Means For Shareholders","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/consumer-durables/nyse-pii/polaris/news/what-polaris-piis-raised-guidance-means-for-shareholders","date":"2026-11-01","timestamp":1793553890.592,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.735,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"Earnings Beat: Here's What Polaris Inc. (NYSE:PII) Analysts Are Forecasting For Next Year","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/consumer-durables/nyse-pii/polaris/news/earnings-beat-heres-what-polaris-inc-nysepii-analysts-are-fo","date":"2026-10-31","timestamp":1793456265.799,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"PII Q3 deep dive: operational efficiency, utility demand, and margin headwinds shape outlook","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/a